completion.summary:
Every queue pause now records a typed reason with its time:
- a failed or exited mailbox turn;
- provider capacity;
- a Stop, through master's pause_queue_for_operator_stop helper;
- an unresolved Codex terminal;
- a source-observation hold;
- a failed human start;
- a failed runtime reset or cleanup;
- a failed save.

What a failed turn's reason carries:
- A bounded failure kind, taken only from typed provider signals: Claude's API status or Codex's codexErrorInfo.
- A one-line summary under an allowlist rule: plain-prose words are kept up to the first non-plain word or credential label, then the rest becomes [redacted]. The summary is bounded to 120 characters, is computed before the state lock, and has a stated best-effort residual.

Where the reason shows:
- It persists with the paused state and clears when the pause lifts.
- termal_list_sessions shows queuePaused and queuePauseReason for local sessions.
- The exact read's current status carries recipientQueuePause for local and same-host domain messages.
- Strict StateSessionSummary rows are unchanged; the reasons travel in a StateResponse side map.

Cross-host propagation is out of scope, tracked as w-97d616820a66. Criterion 1, the cause of the 2026-11-23 stall, is recorded on the item.

Landed as 082fb430 on master. Review pair R13-1 was clean. Landing FULLs passed on Linux (test-4ee47b80) and Windows (test-e05a689a). The independent acceptance evaluation (delegation-2358d1ea) passed both criteria.
